+Veneer's `elements` layer sits after `base`, so Tailwind's reset arrives under Veneer's own element
+treatment rather than over it: every property Veneer declares for an overlapping element keeps the
+value the standalone cascade resolves for it, and what the `preflight` profile adds is the
+properties Veneer leaves alone. [The preflight pairing](../tests/tailwind/preflight.test.ts) derives
+the overlap — the tags the compiled `base` layer's type selectors name, intersected with the tags
+Veneer's elements partials style — renders one neutral element per tag, and reads every property
+that layer declares before and after the profile loads. Each property Veneer's own rules declare for
+the tag is asserted unchanged, and each property that moved is a row of the following table.
+
+The border style and the tab size move on every overlapping element, because the reset's universal
+rule declares them: it sets a border style the elements never paint, because it sets the border
+width to zero beside it, and it lowers the tab size. The rest of the rows are the form controls and
+the document root, which preflight resets to inherit the page's own font, color, and background.
